  "label": "Shower Metaphor",
  "description": "The phrase 'shower' is used metaphorically to represent cleansing, release, or emotional/physical purification. In this context, it refers to a necessary but unpleasant experience — often used in discussions of trauma, systemic injustice, or personal hardship. The metaphor is culturally embedded in Western discourse, particularly in contexts of mental health, social commentary, and political resistance.",
